                        {
                          "String": "The existing information was reviewed by the independent Expert Panel for Fragrance Safety and supports the use of Myristic acid as described in this fragrance ingredient safety assessment. Data for myristic acid and from read-across analog palmitic acid  show that Myristic acid is not expected to be genotoxic. The repeated dose toxicity, reproductive toxicity, and local respiratory toxicity endpoints were evaluated using the Threshold of Toxicological Concern (TTC) for a Cramer Class I material, and the exposures are below the TTC for these endpoints. Data for myristic acid and for read-across analog nonionic acid show that there are no safety concerns for skin sensitization under the current declared levels of use. Myristic acid is not expected to be photoirritating/photoallergenic based on evaluation of the ultraviolet/visible (UV/Vis) spectra.",
